[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd" :question/id #uuid "01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-185123" :question/problem "$(-70)^{2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To work out $(-70)^{2},$ we multiply $-70$ by itself:\n\n$$\n(-70)^{2}=(-70)\\cdot (-70)=4,900\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer/id #uuid "971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4900" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078611 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624" :question/id #uuid "454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624" :question/math-academy-id "q-75596" :question/problem "What is the constant term in the expression $\\frac{2}{3}+6a-4b?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms: $\\frac{2}{3}$, $6a$, and $-4b.$  The only term that does not contain any variables is $\\frac{2}{3}$, so $\\frac{2}{3}$ is the constant term." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" "answer-3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" "answer-7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" "answer-df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" :answer/id #uuid "59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" :answer/id #uuid "3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" :answer/id #uuid "7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" :answer/id #uuid "df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer/id #uuid "7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179814 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308" :question/id #uuid "e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308" :question/math-academy-id "q-186120" :question/problem "$1.2-5=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $5$ is larger than $1.2,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction in the reverse order:\n\n$$\n5-1.2=3.8\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n1.2-5=-3.8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162" :answer-field/id #uuid "f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer/id #uuid "dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6" :question/id #uuid "34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-155548" :question/problem "![](images/86/867e0d53894e1cacac86120e5c79b32071e2b0a4863b445e6d3492392a59461d.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,Q,J$\n\nII. $P,O,L$\n\nIII. $L,O,M$" :question/worked-solution "- $M,Q,J$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/7f/7f707d8fbeb9853ccb9441bbdab3b0674c5f51da7f73da73d73ee6592dca04ea.png)\n\n- $P,O,L$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/02/028ae56c8a85699d4d6719df2f80a989f1271e392546d005093319af2365675d.png)\n\n \n\n- $L,O,M$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/bf/bf0579ecbc33ebe2d97dc1b305de0a89b0c22dadd6a11d0e88ac4a36acbd447f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" "answer-af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" "answer-5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" "answer-85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" :answer/id #uuid "09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" :answer/id #uuid "af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" :answer/id #uuid "5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" :answer/id #uuid "85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer/id #uuid "46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073899 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773" :question/id #uuid "23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773" :question/math-academy-id "q-160597" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(0,2)$  and $(0,5)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/f3/f329376e27ec08d2695db0e6d007e7a7b5342e7737c5d3f45eb524a2b1c2e572.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/66/66543bc73667ed70a965db4af2e657ad991660fc1b3a73a6e585943deffd3bbb.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/5d/5ded01b570e62d1e206aa8abd1012121367e60e749d441eb4e6ec7e3b12f6e8a.png)\n\nThe point $(0,5)$ is at a distance of $5$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(0,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $5-2=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" "answer-b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" "answer-79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" "answer-22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" :answer/id #uuid "78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer/id #uuid "8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" :answer/id #uuid "b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" :answer/id #uuid "79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c" :answer/id #uuid "22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105756 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5" :question/id #uuid "8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117935" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e1675e22ef33aa40b96349c910f04178dd4b11b1e7e97f15a5314977eea914f.png)\n\nWhich vertices are adjacent to $F?$" :question/worked-solution "$F$ is the endpoint of the sides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}.$ Therefore, the vertices $E$ and $G$ are adjacent to $F.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" "answer-02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" "answer-4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" "answer-6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" :answer/id #uuid "e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $D$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" :answer/id #uuid "02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" :answer/id #uuid "4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $E$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" :answer/id #uuid "6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer/id #uuid "dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$E$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064358 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/id #uuid "61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/math-academy-id "q-181162" :question/problem "The value of $12÷(-5),$ expressed as an **improper fraction** in lowest terms, is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(12)$ by a negative one $(-5).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $5$ without any signs: $12÷5=\\frac{12}{5}.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/id #uuid "3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147595 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/id #uuid "21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/math-academy-id "q-169408" :question/problem "Anna makes two cakes. The first cake weighs $1,200\\,\\text{g},$ while the second cake weighs $140%$ of the weight of the first. What is the weight of the second cake?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the first cake, which is $1,200\\,\\text{g}.$ The percentage is $140%,$ and the part is the weight of the second cake.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140%=140÷100=1.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140%=\\frac{140}{100}=\\frac{140÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{1,200}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 240 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" "answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" "answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" "answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/id #uuid "3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,500\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/id #uuid "68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,680\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/id #uuid "f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,720\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/id #uuid "c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,800\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/id #uuid "f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,940\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054779 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/id #uuid "9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171509" :question/problem "$8(2u-5v)=${{field-1}}\n$u\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$" :question/worked-solution "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(2u-5v) & = \\\\ 8\\cdot 2u+8\\cdot (-5v) & = \\\\ (16u)+(-40v) & = \\\\ 16u-40v\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" "answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/id #uuid "1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/id #uuid "e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/id #uuid "72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119548" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(1\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{2-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/fd/fd7fc3fedd2dbf8c90592bbedfdc15181eae63e4d2cbd71a4c036b2d75e8921c.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-4}{3}=\\frac{-2}{3}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/id #uuid "43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" "answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" "answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" "answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/id #uuid "6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/id #uuid "233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/id #uuid "975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/id #uuid "b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/id #uuid "6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074391 :question/problem "There are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks in a zoo. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ ducks." :question/worked-solution "Since there are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks, the ratio of parrots to ducks is $18:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,18 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,6 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $6:5$ is equivalent to $18:15.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:5\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $5\\,$ ducks.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186072584 :answer-field/correct 17592186072586 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152870 :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $1$\n\nII. $-2$\n\nIII. $-\\frac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $1$ and $-2$ are integers, but $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151727 :answer-field/correct 17592186151731 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078507 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/id #uuid "c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101757" :question/problem "What are the like terms in the expression $10x-18y-7z+10?$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(10x)+(-18y)+(-7z)+(10).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/id #uuid "df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" "answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" "answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" "answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/id #uuid "cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-18y$ and $-7z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/id #uuid "b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-18y$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/id #uuid "8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-7z$ and $10x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/id #uuid "430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10x$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/id #uuid "74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No like terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/id #uuid "33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/math-academy-id "q-85461" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $11\\,289\\,643$\n\nII. $13\\,298\\,784$\n\nIII. $215\\,153\\,238$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $11\\,289\\,643$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+2+9+8+7+8+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+1+5+1+5+3+2+3+8=30\n$$\n\nSo, $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" "answer-2