r-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/choices "answer-6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040"] ["answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/choices "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a"] ["question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8"] [17592186105756 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5"] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/id #uuid "61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524"] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/math-academy-id "q-181162"] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/problem "The value of $12÷(-5),$ expressed as an **improper fraction** in lowest terms, is{{field-1}}."] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(12)$ by a negative one $(-5).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $5$ without any signs: $12÷5=\\frac{12}{5}.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$"] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973"] ["answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/id #uuid "3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0"] ["answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}"] ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/correct "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0"] ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/choices "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0"] ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973"] [17592186064358 :knowledge-point/questions "question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/id #uuid "21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/math-academy-id "q-169408"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/problem "Anna makes two cakes. The first cake weighs $1,200\\,\\text{g},$ while the second cake weighs $140%$ of the weight of the first. What is the weight of the second cake?"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the first cake, which is $1,200\\,\\text{g}.$ The percentage is $140%,$ and the part is the weight of the second cake.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140%=140÷100=1.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140%=\\frac{140}{100}=\\frac{140÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{1,200}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 240 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818"] ["answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/id #uuid "3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe"] ["answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/value "1,500\\,\\text{g}"] ["answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/id #uuid "68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d"] ["answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/value "1,680\\,\\text{g}"] ["answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/id #uuid "f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b"] ["answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/value "1,720\\,\\text{g}"] ["answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/id #uuid "c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00"] ["answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/value "1,800\\,\\text{g}"] ["answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/id #uuid "f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206"] ["answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/value "1,940\\,\\text{g}"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/correct "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/choices "answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/choices "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/choices "answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/choices "answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00"] ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/choices "answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206"] ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818"] [17592186147595 :knowledge-point/questions "question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/id #uuid "9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171509"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/problem "$8(2u-5v)=${{field-1}}\n$u\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/worked-solution "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(2u-5v) & = \\\\ 8\\cdot 2u+8\\cdot (-5v) & = \\\\ (16u)+(-40v) & = \\\\ 16u-40v\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e"] ["answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/id #uuid "1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd"] ["answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/value "16"] ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/correct "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd"] ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/choices "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd"] ["answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b"] ["answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/id #uuid "e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8"] ["answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/value "40"] ["answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/correct "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8"] ["answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/choices "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e"] ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b"] [17592186054779 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/id #uuid "72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119548"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{3}.$"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(1\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{2-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/fd/fd7fc3fedd2dbf8c90592bbedfdc15181eae63e4d2cbd71a4c036b2d75e8921c.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-4}{3}=\\frac{-2}{3}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/id #uuid "43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6"] ["answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/id #uuid "6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05"] ["answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/id #uuid "233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa"] ["answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/id #uuid "975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed"] ["answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/id #uuid "b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4"] ["answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}"] ["answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/id #uuid "6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44"] ["answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/correct "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/choices "answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/choices "answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/choices "answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4"] ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/choices "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44"] ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6"] [17592186179699 :knowledge-point/questions "question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f"] [17592186074391 :question/problem "There are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks in a zoo. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ ducks."] [17592186074391 :question/worked-solution "Since there are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks, the ratio of parrots to ducks is $18:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,18 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,6 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $6:5$ is equivalent to $18:15.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:5\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $5\\,$ ducks.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$"] [17592186074391 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186072584 :answer-field/correct 17592186072586] [17592186152870 :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $1$\n\nII. $-2$\n\nIII. $-\\frac{1}{2}$"] [17592186152870 :question/worked-solution "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $1$ and $-2$ are integers, but $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] [17592186152870 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186151727 :answer-field/correct 17592186151731] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/id #uuid "c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9"] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101757"] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/problem "What are the like terms in the expression $10x-18y-7z+10?$"] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(10x)+(-18y)+(-7z)+(10).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression."] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/id #uuid "df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a"] ["answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/id #uuid "cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b"] ["answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/value "$-18y$ and $-7z$"] ["answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/id #uuid "b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45"] ["answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/value "$-18y$ and $10$"] ["answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/id #uuid "8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91"] ["answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/value "$-7z$ and $10x$"] ["answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/id #uuid "430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01"] ["answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/value "$10x$ and $10$"] ["answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/id #uuid "74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86"] ["answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/value "No like terms"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/correct "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/choices "answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/choices "answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/choices "answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/choices "answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01"] ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/choices "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86"] ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a"] [17592186078507 :knowledge-point/questions "question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9"] ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/id #uuid "33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22"] ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/math-academy-id "q-85461"] ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $11\\,289\\,643$\n\nII. $13\\,298\\,784$\n\nIII. $215\\,153\\,238$"] ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $11\\,289\\,643$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+2+9+8+7+8+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+1+5+1+5+3+2+3+8=30\n$$\n\nSo, $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915"] ["answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" :answer/id #uuid "9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2"] ["answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" :answer/id #uuid "2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce"] ["answer-2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer/id #uuid "bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4"] ["answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" :answer/id #uuid "6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361"] ["answer-6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" :answer/value "II only"] ["answe